rican horsesickness in the western Cape: application of a F(ab')2-based indirect ELISA.</article-title><source>Onderstepoort J Vet Res</source><volume>58</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2052314</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005997-Roy2"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roy</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bishop</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Howard</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Aitchison</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Erasmus</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Recombinant baculovirus-synthesized African horsesickness virus (AHSV) outer-capsid protein VP2 provides protection against virulent AHSV challenge.</article-title><source>J Gen Virol</source><volume>77(Pt 9)</volume><fpage>2053</fpage><lpage>2057</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8811002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005997-Kundig1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kundig</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalberer</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hengartner</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Zinkernagel</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Vaccination with two different vaccinia recombinant viruses: long-term inhibition of secondary vaccination.</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>1154</fpage><lpage>1158</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8249436</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005997-Rocha1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rocha</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Caetano</surname>